JLS 12.4.2 on the linear-memory wasm target: a class's initializer ran its <clinit> without initializing its
superclass first, so a subclass initialized before its superclass whenever the subclass was touched first (TeaVM's
C target generates the same initializer shape). Minecraft numbers entity data fields per class in static
initializers by walking superclasses (ClassTreeIdRegistry), so LivingEntity took ids from 0 before Entity had
defined its own: "Duplicate id value for 0!" when the first player was created. The generated initializer now
calls the nearest ancestor's initializer (the closest superclass with a <clinit>) after marking its class and
before its own <clinit>.
Codegen: one call in each class initializer that has an initializing ancestor; nothing on paths after initialization.

